cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below. If you cite a measured figure, cite the commit and the split it came from."
title: "Project JAEGER: BCC Re-Investigation Machinery — the forensic layer that keeps claims tied to documents."
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: CDDL-1.1
type: software
abstract: >-
  JAEGER is the BCC Re-Investigation machinery: the forensic layer that
  keeps an investigation's claims tied to the documents they rest on, and
  the gate that decides what may leave the machine. It is NOT the therapeutic
  agent in this tree — that is a SEPARATE project, Project Nurse Ratchet.
  JAEGER provides the evidence provenance, entity resolution, claim-to-source
  citation, and disclosure control for the BCC investigation.
authors:
  - name: "Project JAEGER contributors"
keywords:
  - forensic investigation
  - evidence provenance
  - BCC re-investigation
  - disclosure control
  - claim-to-source citation
  - reproducible verification
  - open science
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Project ELIZA"
    notes: "Sibling forensic investigation suite in the Azazael tree."
    url: "https://github.com/myzticalbabe/azazael/tree/main/Project_ELIZA"
  - type: software
    title: "Project Nurse Ratchet"
    notes: "Separate therapeutic agent project."
    url: "https://github.com/myzticalbabe/azazael/tree/main/Project_Nurse_Ratchet"